Match WcWidth test expectations to go-runewidth 0.0.30.

Guix provides go-runewidth 0.0.30, whose StringWidth sums rune widths within
each grapheme cluster, capped at two cells.  The WcWidth expectations for
flags and an ASCII character followed by a halfwidth voiced sound mark
must reflect those two-cell widths.  The separate GraphemeWidth tests
exercise clipperhouse/displaywidth's results.

Source: https://github.com/mattn/go-runewidth/blob/v0.0.30/runewidth.go#L517-L529

diff --git a/ansi/method_test.go b/ansi/method_test.go
--- a/ansi/method_test.go
+++ b/ansi/method_test.go
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ func TestMethod_StringWidth(t *testing.T) {
 		{"wide chars grapheme width", GraphemeWidth, "コンニチハ", 10},
 		{"emoji wcwidth", WcWidth, "😀", 2},
 		{"emoji grapheme width", GraphemeWidth, "😀", 2},
-		{"flag emoji wcwidth", WcWidth, "🏳️‍🌈", 1},
+		{"flag emoji wcwidth", WcWidth, "🏳️‍🌈", 2},
 		{"flag emoji grapheme width", GraphemeWidth, "🏳️‍🌈", 2},
 	}
 	for _, tt := range tests {
